  "memo": "R08 holds because the shipping address links three accounts. The household exception does not apply because this is not the account's home address. Linkage is the only adverse family present; no earlier outcome settles the order. Row §6.6(b) initially requires identity verification, but the completed id_check failed, making §5.3(b) decisive. Recommend standard escalation, blocking the account and policy-defined linked accounts. The order has already shipped, so the loss stands. A legitimate gift to a shared destination remains plausible, but the failed verification outweighs that explanation. No further check is needed; this evidence does not identify the precise fraud mechanism."
